{
  "scope": "User requested IEC 62351-3 TLS corrections on 2026-10-26 and 2026-10-27; transport security and published CRL replacement. Authorized Tespro deployments are recorded in lab/tg544-openwrt/deploy-manifests.",
  "changes": [
    "Exactly the four mandatory TLS 1.2 cipher suites; conditional NULL and optional AES-256 suites stay disabled",
    "RSA >=2048 and secp256r1 ECDSA support, SHA-256 required/preferred, and policy controls for optional SHA-384/SHA-512",
    "RSA key-length alarms and SHA-1 deprecation warning with strict rejection",
    "Reject absent ClientHello signature_algorithms before server signing on initial handshakes and renegotiations; warn and alarm on the provider SHA-1 fallback",
    "Strict local/peer chain validation and key pairing; pins preserve verification errors",
    "Per-certificate 8,192-octet DER maximum on local and peer TLS chains, with a required alarm and handshake rejection above the limit",
    "MMS and IEC 104 peer-certificate absence, endpoint-identity failure, and authorized-CA individual-certificate alarms",
    "Repeatable IEC 104 exact-certificate pins in addition to mandatory issuer-chain validation",
    "Connection-owned authenticated CRL refresh and idle revocation checks",
    "Expired authenticated CRLs warn without blocking listener startup or ending established sessions; initial peer verification still enforces CRL freshness",
    "Bounded monotonic renegotiation with 30-second completion deadline",
    "Full handshakes until safe peer identity restoration on resumption is implemented",
    "MMS and IEC 104 TLS security events"
  ],
  "remaining_gaps": [
    "OCSP stapling and direct OCSP retrieval",
    "Authenticated automatic CRL distribution",
    "Re-enabling safe session resumption",
    "Device/independent conformance validation"
  ],
